cff-version: 1.2.0
title: FrontierLLM Constitution Corpus
message: >-
  If you use this corpus, please cite it and the Digital Judiciary programme
  papers it instantiates.
type: dataset
version: 2.4.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
license-url: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
authors:
  - family-names: Kadambi
    given-names: Arun
  - family-names: Kuppuswamy
    given-names: Venkat
    affiliation: >-
      D'Amore-McKim School of Business, Northeastern University
abstract: >-
  An open 6,000-case conformance corpus for governing software change at a
  frontier large-language-model developer under a Digital Judiciary: a
  constitution of 113 provisions (22 absolute) spanning model and prompt bills
  of materials, training-data provenance and opt-out, personal data, agent
  identity and agent-authored code, LLM-specific security, probabilistic
  evaluation and contamination, frontier safety and weight security, inference
  latency and determinism, financial guardrails, brand safety, IP
  contamination, classic software supply chain, application security and
  governance of the judiciary itself. Every provision carries a status —
  in force, deferred, or advisory — and a provision that is not in force may
  never be marked absolute. Ground truth is computed from an executed trace
  rather than authored. Ships a reference adjudication engine, 26 conformance
  checks, a mutation matrix, and a three-pack profile comparison against the
  VetPOC and SemiFab corpora.
keywords:
  - compliance
  - precedent
  - policy-as-code
  - frontier AI
  - AI governance
  - EU AI Act
  - model provenance
  - conformance testing
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      When Retrieval Binds: Appraisal, Authenticity and Disposition in
      Automated Compliance Decisions
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Case-Base Formation for Precedential Constraint: Standing, Admission
      Rules, and the Reason Model
    authors:
      - family-names: Kadambi
        given-names: Arun
      - family-names: Kuppuswamy
        given-names: Venkat
